"""rl-readiness R3 -- GRPO smoke of Qwen3-14B LoRA on Kaggle T4.

Pre-reg: kaggle/PREREG-RL-READINESS.md section R3 (frozen 2026-09-28).
Question: does TRL GRPOTrainer (via unsloth) run Qwen3-14B 4-bit LoRA on ONE T4
at group size G >= 4 (target 8) with completions >= 1024 tokens, with a REAL
reward (netlist round-trip on every rollout + in-kernel SPICE sizing on a few)?
Decision rule: "GRPO-on-Kaggle feasible" if a G>=4, >=1024-token step completes
without OOM; report rollouts/GPU-h and the implied architecture-B round size.

Flow (every phase time-guarded, R3_BUDGET_MIN total):
  0. env log: nvidia-smi, nproc / os.cpu_count / CPU model, RAM, disk.
  1. clone the repo PINNED at REPO_SHA (circuit-repro-ghtoken dataset) +
     kaggle/bootstrap.sh (ngspice 47 from the circuit-repro-ngspice47 dataset).
  2. CLEAN in-kernel SPICE timing (nothing else running): smoke_run
     (kaggle/bench_anchor_prep.py) of v1a anchors at 1 seed x 300 evals, pdk
     bptm45 -- serial, stability-gated, 1x600, and nproc-parallel.
  3. pip-install the E-e unsloth stack (torch untouched via constraints);
     pre-download the model; in the BACKGROUND build a --system-site-packages
     venv with vllm (torch-2.10-compatible release) for unsloth fast_inference.
  4. GRPO trials, each its own subprocess on ONE T4 (CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES), two
     GPUs = two parallel trial queues:
       H-G8-L1024  HF generation, G=8, 1024 forced tokens, 3 steps (MAIN)
       H-G4-L1024  HF generation, G=4 (fallback point / G scaling)
       V-*         unsloth fast_inference (vLLM colocated) when the venv is ready
       H-G8-L2048, H-G16-L1024  OOM-boundary probes (only if the MAIN passed)
     "forced" = min_new_tokens = max_completion_length (EOS suppressed), so every
     step is a true >=1024-token step (worst case for memory and time).
     Rewards: reward_valid (proposal.round_trip, every rollout), reward_novel
     (WL hash != anchor), reward_spice (smoke_run 1x300 bptm45 on up to
     N_SPICE valid+novel rollouts per step, parallel CPU pool; 0 for the rest).
  5. summary.json; big files stay in /tmp; ngspice prefix removed from output.

Prompts: real arm-B editcap prompts (k=1) from the OLD library
kaggle/editcap-lib-v1a (non-bench), embedded below (build_prompts.py). The
kernel re-checks the held-out fence against the clone's editcap-lib-v12-*.
"""
